    description: "Version 1.0.1"
url: "https://sr-dash.github.io/heliofield/observations.html"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sr-dash/heliofield-imagery"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A nightly pipeline that, for each HelioField coronal-field product and for
  one day per Carrington rotation since May 2010, takes the image nearest the
  map time from SDO/AIA and HMI, SOHO/LASCO C2 and C3, STEREO-A/EUVI and Solar
  Orbiter/EUI and PHI, turns it solar north up, and stores it with the
  observer's Carrington position, distance and plate scale so the model's
  field lines can be drawn from each spacecraft's viewpoint. Each image comes
  in a standard and an enhanced rendering: the WOW filter for disk images, and
  for LASCO the ratio to a minimum background (NRL's real-time method) and the
  NRGF filter.
keywords:
  - heliophysics
  - solar physics
  - SDO
  - SOHO
  - LASCO
  - STEREO
  - Solar Orbiter
  - coronal magnetic field
  - space weather
